% PROVENANCE WARNING, recorded here rather than silently corrected elsewhere:
% the reference this repository calls "Stangeby 2022, Nucl. Fusion 62"
% (src/validation/grid.py:29 and :69; outputs/CH5_EVIDENCE.md:74;
% outputs/findings_10_four_agent_review.md:121; the [SOURCE REQUIRED] marker at
% thesis_tex/chapter5_C5D.tex:289) is in fact Nucl. Fusion 63, 016017 (2023).
% The DOI recorded in grid.py is correct; the volume and year are not. The key
% below is therefore Stangeby2023. Anyone who has written \cite{Stangeby2022}
% should repoint it rather than a duplicate entry being added.
%
% SECOND WARNING: the n_e,sep ~ 6e19 m^-3 band quoted from Stangeby part B
% appears there as a block quotation from its own reference [1], which is
% Pitts et al. (2019). Pitts2019 is the primary source and is included below.
% Pitts's n_e,sep is an outboard-midplane quantity while Stangeby's n_e,u is
% an X-point quantity, and part B records that the two differ
% (3.98e19 vs 5.94e19 m^-3 on the same flux tube). Any sentence calling a
% single band "the upstream separatrix density" is eliding that distinction.
%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

